# 8. RSS News Cards Must Survive Updates and Return After Live RSS Sync

Existing RSS news cards disappear from the Home Feed after application updates. However, clicking “लाइव RSS सिंक करें” causes the channel's stories to appear again.

This suggests that the Home Feed may be relying on stale local state, seed data, incomplete persistence, or an incorrect startup merge strategy.

### Required changes

- Audit the complete RSS lifecycle: source configuration, fetching, article normalization, persistence, startup loading, synchronization, and Home Feed rendering.
- Identify why existing RSS articles disappear after an update or reload.
- Ensure currently configured and authorized RSS sources remain persisted across application updates.
- Ensure previously fetched articles that should remain visible are stored and reloaded correctly.
- On startup, load valid persisted RSS articles before applying any fallback or seed data.
- Do not overwrite a valid populated feed with empty or stale seed data.
- Ensure “लाइव RSS सिंक करें” fetches and merges new articles without unnecessarily removing existing valid cards.
- Deduplicate stories using a stable article identifier, canonical URL, or another suitable existing identifier.
- Update articles when appropriate without creating duplicate cards.
- Respect the existing retention, removal, and source-authorization rules.
- Preserve RSS links and configurations saved by the existing Admin/Master Admin.
- Show meaningful errors if synchronization fails instead of silently clearing the Home Feed.

Seed data may be used only as a legitimate initial fallback when no valid persisted data exists. It must not replace existing production content.

**Acceptance criteria:** Save RSS sources, fetch articles, refresh the page, restart the application, and simulate a normal update. Previously persisted eligible cards remain visible. Running live RSS sync adds or updates stories without erasing valid existing stories.

